<!DOCTYPE topic SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       id="Custom-Data-Types" title="Custom Data Types">

    <title>
        Custom Data Types
    </title>
    <p>If you want to create a custom type, create a variable typed as <code>SqlType&lt;T&gt;</code>, where
        <code>T</code> is your custom data
        type, then set it to a new <code>SqlType&lt;&gt;()</code> and implement the <code>bind</code> and
        <code>read</code> functions.</p>
    <p>Here is how DimensionPause implements the <code>SqlType</code> for <code>Instant</code>, while supporting
        nullability as well</p>
    <code-block lang="java">
public static final SqlType&lt;Instant&gt; INSTANT = new SqlType&lt;&gt;() {
    public void bind(PreparedStatement ps, int index, Instant value) throws SQLException {
        if (value != null) ps.setLong(4, value.toEpochMilli());
        else ps.setNull(4, Types.BIGINT);
    }

    public @Nullable Instant read(ResultSet rs, String column) throws SQLException {
        Object raw = rs.getObject(column);
        Long expiresAtMs = (raw instanceof Number n) ? n.longValue() : null;
        return expiresAtMs != null ? Instant.ofEpochMilli(expiresAtMs) : null;
    }
};
</code-block>
    <p>Since SQLite has no idea what an <code>Instant</code> is, we use <code>BIGINT</code> as the backing data type.
        Think of <code>bind()</code> as a
        serializer and <code>read()</code> as a deserializer: <code>bind()</code> writes a <code>long</code> to the DB,
        and <code>read()</code> converts it back to an
        <code>Instant</code>, or returns null if the column is null.</p>

</topic>